  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At San Cha Mountain, Mo Wu Tian lists King Quan, Wang Er Gou’s, share of the three kings inheritance and pairs Ying Ming with Ba Huang.",
      "chapters": [
        391
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_san_cha_mountain",
        "char_mo_wu_tian",
        "char_king_quan",
        "char_wang_er",
        "fac_three_kings",
        "char_ba_huang"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Bai Ning Bing commands it out as the second dog emperor against Xiao Mang. It is the size of a normal dog beast. There are gorgeous patterns on its snowy white skin like pink cherry blossoms. Wild Gu form clouds under its feet so it can fly.",
      "chapters": [
        394
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_bai_ning_bing",
        "char_xiao_mang",
        "sys_wild_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "While Ying Ming blocks his path, Xiao Mang grows anxious that Tie clan will take the immortal treasure.",
      "chapters": [
        397
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "path-to-bronze-hall",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_tie_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Xiao Mang and Mo Wu Tian push near the bronze hall again, Ba Huang and Ying Ming block their advance as before.",
      "chapters": [
        403
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "second-blockade",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later groups Ba Huang and Ying Ming of the three kings inheritance as two beast emperors whose battle strength can match rank five Gu Masters, able to obstruct Mo Wu Tian and Xiao Mang for a time.",
      "chapters": [
        409
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "beast-emperor",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan recalls that Ying Ming and Ba Huang, the dog emperors he used in the three kings blessed land, held off rank five Gu Masters, then notes he was busy escaping and does not know whether they were killed in battle or taken in by others.",
      "chapters": [
        491
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "after-three-kings",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Beside Ye Fan, Fang Yuan recognizes the dog emperor as Ying Ming from Three Kings blessed land, notes that it survived and now follows Ye Fan, and treats that fact as absent from Biography of Ye Fan.",
      "chapters": [
        681
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "beside-ye-fan",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ye_fan"
      ]
    }
  ],
